{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative","title":"def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.md","line":300,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex#def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","label":"def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative","line":666,"source":"\\begin{definition}[the exterior derivative $d^\\nabla h$ of a symmetric tensor]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0363}\n  If $h(z,w)=g(H(z),w)$ is symmetric, then the connection exterior derivative\n  is defined by\n  \\[\n    d^\\nabla h(X,Y,Z)=(\\nabla_Xh)(Y,Z)-(\\nabla_Yh)(X,Z).\n  \\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[the exterior derivative <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d^\\nabla h$\">$d^\\nabla h$</span> of a symmetric tensor] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368392d636f64617a7a692d6578746572696f722d64657269766174697665\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0363</span></span> If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h(z,w)=g(H(z),w)$\">$h(z,w)=g(H(z),w)$</span> is symmetric, then the connection exterior derivative is defined by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  d^\\nabla h(X,Y,Z)=(\\nabla _Xh)(Y,Z)-(\\nabla _Yh)(X,Z).  \\]\">\\[  d^\\nabla h(X,Y,Z)=(\\nabla _Xh)(Y,Z)-(\\nabla _Yh)(X,Z).  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechniqu